<div class="container page-body"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE NOTEBOOK</p><h1>Hi, I’m Ravindra.<br>I learn by <em>building.</em></h1><p>And by writing down the things I wish someone had explained a little more clearly.</p></header><div class="about-grid"><div class="prose"><p>I’m Ravindra Kumar, a cloud and platform engineer working with Kubernetes, infrastructure as code, and delivery automation.</p><p>The Code Clouds is my independent space for practical technology writing: the commands worth remembering, the concepts worth slowing down for, and the small lessons that make the next project a little better.</p><h2>What you’ll find here</h2><ul><li>Focused guides on cloud, Kubernetes, Terraform, and DevOps.</li><li>Clear prerequisites, concrete examples, and links to original documentation.</li><li>Learning resources and course offers with transparent disclosures.</li></ul><h2>A note on independence</h2><p>The writing here represents my own perspective, not my employer’s. Examples are educational: adapt them to your environment and review the impact before running commands.</p><h2>Let’s compare notes</h2><p>Have a correction, a topic suggestion, or an approved course offer to share? <a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reach me on LinkedIn</a>. There is no submission form collecting your personal details here.</p><p>If you came looking for my earlier personal site, the <a href="/portfolio/">original portfolio is still available</a>.</p></div><aside class="profile-card"><span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">RK</span><h2>Ravindra Kumar</h2><p>Cloud · Platform engineering · DevOps</p><a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a><a href="{{ site.github }}" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore my GitHub ↗</a><a href="/portfolio/">View original portfolio ↗</a><a href="/feed.xml">Follow the writing via RSS ↗</a></aside></div></div>
